<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="[scrollbar-gutter:stable]">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="csrf-token" content={get_csrf_token()} />
    <.live_title default="WoW Forever Recipe Finder" suffix=" · Recipe Finder">
      {assigns[:page_title]}
    </.live_title>
    <%!-- Deliberately NOT routed through the ~p sigil: Phoenix's static-
    manifest digest substitution rewrites ~p"/favicon.svg" to its
    content-hashed filename (e.g. favicon-<hash>.svg) in production,
    but Plug.Static's `only:` allowlist (WowForeverRecipeFinderWeb.
    static_paths/0) matches the literal "favicon.svg"/"favicon.ico"
    strings exactly — the hashed filename doesn't match either entry,
    so Plug.Static refuses to serve it and the request 404s. Confirmed
    live: the previous ?v=2 cache-bust attempt (combined with ~p's own
    digest substitution) produced a broken double-query href that
    404'd in production the whole time — not a browser-caching issue
    at all, despite looking like one. Plain literal paths bypass the
    digest step entirely and are always served (they're on the exact-
    match allowlist); ?v=3 is our own manual cache-bust, bumped once
    to force a re-fetch for any client that cached the 404. --%>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg?v=3" />
    <link rel="alternate icon" href="/favicon.ico?v=3" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="" />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,500;0,9..144,600;0,9..144,700;1,9..144,500&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/app.css"} />
    <script defer phx-track-static type="text/javascript" src={~p"/assets/app.js"}>
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    {@inner_content}
  </body>
</html>
